{"symbol":"EPHA2","resolved":{"input":"EPHA2","symbol":"EPHA2","ncbi_gene_id":"1969","name":"EPH receptor A2","location":"1p36.13","aliases":["ARCC2","CTPA","CTPP1","CTRCT6","ECK"],"uniprot":"P29317","uniprot_reviewed":true},"function":[{"text":"EPHA2 function (UniProt P29317, UniProt evidence code ECO:0000269): Receptor tyrosine kinase which binds promiscuously membrane-bound ephrin-A family ligands residing on adjacent cells, leading to contact-dependent bidirectional signaling into neighboring cells. The signaling pathway downstream of the receptor is referred to as forward signaling while the signaling pathway downstream of the ephrin ligand is referred to as reverse signaling. Activated by the ligand ephrin-A1/EFNA1 regulates migration, integrin-mediated adhesion, proliferation and differentiation of cells. Regulates cell adhesion and differentiation through DSG1/desmoglein-1 and inhibition of the ERK1/ERK2 (MAPK3/MAPK1, respectively) signaling pathway. May also participate in UV ...","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P29317","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P29317/entry","title":"EPHA2: Ephrin type-A receptor 2"},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:10655584","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10655584/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:16236711","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16236711/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:18339848","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18339848/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:19573808","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/19573808/","title":""}]},{"text":"EPHA2 function (UniProt P29317, UniProt evidence code ECO:0000269): (Microbial infection) Acts as a receptor for hepatitis C virus (HCV) in hepatocytes and facilitates its cell entry. Mediates HCV entry by promoting the formation of the CD81-CLDN1 receptor complexes that are essential for HCV entry and by enhancing membrane fusion of cells expressing HCV envelope glycoproteins","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P29317","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P29317/entry","title":"EPHA2: Ephrin type-A receptor 2"},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:21516087","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21516087/","title":""}]}],"go":[{"text":"EPHA2 GO biological process annotations: cAMP metabolic process, cell chemotaxis, cell migration, cell motility, ephrin receptor signaling pathway, intrinsic apoptotic signaling pathway in response to DNA damage, keratinocyte differentiation, negative regulation of cell adhesion mediated by integrin, positive regulation of bicellular tight junction assembly, positive regulation of cell migration, positive regulation of protein localization to plasma membrane, protein localization to plasma membrane (+3 more)","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P29317","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P29317/entry","title":"EPHA2: Ephrin type-A receptor 2"}]},{"text":"EPHA2 GO biological process annotations: angiogenesis, bone remodeling, branching involved in mammary gland duct morphogenesis, cell surface receptor protein tyrosine kinase signaling pathway, lens fiber cell morphogenesis, mammary gland epithelial cell proliferation, osteoblast differentiation, osteoclast differentiation, regulation of angiogenesis, regulation of blood vessel endothelial cell migration","evidence":"computationally predicted","code":"PRED","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"P29317","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/P29317/entry","title":"EPHA2: Ephrin type-A receptor 2"}]}],"pathways":[{"source":"Reactome","gene":"EPHA2","id":"R-HSA-2682334","name":"EPH-Ephrin signaling","url":"https://reactome.org/content/detail/R-HSA-2682334","evidence":"curated database evidence"},{"source":"Reactome","gene":"EPHA2","id":"R-HSA-3928663","name":"EPHA-mediated growth cone collapse","url":"https://reactome.org/content/detail/R-HSA-39286